---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"; import { affiliates, affiliatesActive, AMAZON_STATEMENT } from "../config/affiliates";
import { SITE_URL } from "../config/site";
import { breadcrumbLd } from "../lib/schema";
const jsonld = breadcrumbLd([{name:'Home',item:`${SITE_URL}/`},{name:'Affiliate disclosure',item:`${SITE_URL}/affiliate-disclosure/`}]);
---
<Base title="Affiliate disclosure | The Fault Code" description="How The Fault Code uses affiliate links, including Amazon Associates, and how they do not affect what the code pages say." jsonld={jsonld}>
<div class="wrap prose"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Affiliate disclosure</li></ol></nav><div class="card" style="margin-top:12px"><h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>{affiliatesActive ? <p>Some links on this site are affiliate links. If you buy something or book a service through one of them, we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. Pages with affiliate links say so near the top and in the footer, and the links are marked as sponsored.</p> : <p>At the moment, no link on this site earns us a commission. If we join affiliate programs in the future, links that earn a commission will be marked as sponsored and this page will say so.</p>}
{affiliates.amazon.enabled && <><h2>Amazon Associates</h2><p>{AMAZON_STATEMENT}</p><p>The "Shop on Amazon" buttons on <a href="/codes/">code pages</a>, <a href="/guides/">field guides</a> and brand pages open Amazon search results for a generic part name, such as "furnace flame sensor" or "washing machine drain hose". <a href="/parts/">Parts and tools pages</a> and the "Parts &amp; tools for this fix" lists on code pages also carry Amazon links. Links labelled "Search" open Amazon search results. A few links go straight to one product page: for those we read the exact product title on Amazon, but we do not claim it fits your model. Neither kind is a product recommendation. Check the part number against your furnace's manual or the old part before you buy, and leave gas valve and other gas-train work to a licensed technician.</p></>}
<p>Affiliate links do not change which codes we list or what we say about them. Code meanings come from the manufacturers' manuals.</p></div></div>
</Base>
